-- Real Estate Taxation (Appreciation and Purchase) Law 5723-1963, s 9: the purchase tax on a residential apartment.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
-- ../../../real-estate-taxation-law-5723-1963/registers/source-bundle/real-estate-taxation-law-5723-1963.he.wiki.txt (sha256 aa4217b3...c1c, Hebrew Wikisource
-- revision 3085765 of 2026-09-30). An unofficial consolidation.
--
-- WHAT IT SAYS. (a) The buyer of a right in land pays purchase tax at a rate of the sale value or a fixed amount, as the Minister fixes by regulations. (c1c)(1) On the
-- sale of a right in a residential apartment from 1 August 2013 the tax is by bands of the value (5%, 6%, 7%, 8%, 10%, the bands printed for 2025). (2) An individual
-- resident in Israel who bought the apartment from 1 August 2013 and for whom one of (a) it is his only apartment, (b) he sold the other apartment that was his only one
-- within 24 months (12 months from the contractor's delivery date), (b1) the delayed purchase-group case, (c) it is a replacement apartment, holds, pays by the bands
-- of (3) (0%, 3.5%, 5%, 8%, 10%). (c1f) For a sale from 28 November 2021 until 31 December 2024 (the consolidation's note: extended to 31 December 2026) of an
-- apartment not under (c1c)(2): 8% up to 6,055,070 and 10% above. (c2) The amounts are adjusted every 16 January, other than in the tax years 2025 to 2027, by the rise of
-- the housing-services index over its value of 15 January 2027, and rounded to the nearest multiple of 5 shillings.
--
-- WHICH SALES IT ANSWERS: from 16 January 2025 on. The amounts the text prints are those "adjusted/stated for 2025" and, by (c2), unchanged for the tax years 2025 to 2027,
-- which run from 16 January 2025 to 15 January 2028 (the table note after (c1c)(3)); the amounts for earlier years are indexed from base months and the indices are not
-- supplied, and the windows (c) to (c1b) of 1995 to July 2013 are not encoded (NOTES.md coverage table). From 16 January 2028 the amounts are adjusted by the index readings
-- the caller supplies (declined if not supplied).
--
-- NOT ENCODED, with the reason: (a) other land (the rates are fixed by regulations, which are not deposited); (b) an action in a land association (the same tax on the
-- proportional part); (c3), (c4), (d) (publication, powers, exemptions); (e) (purchase tax is tax for every purpose); ss 9B, 9C (temporary reductions of 2001-2003).
--
-- FORKS: P1 (the end of the (c1f) period), R2 (rounding a half to a multiple of 5).

§ `Real Estate Taxation Law, s 9 — the purchase tax on a residential apartment`

