GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 9 as deposited states the bands for a sale from 16 January 2025 on` MEANS
    REFUSE "the bands of section 9(c1c) are printed for the tax years 2025 to 2027 only, and for an earlier sale the amounts are indexed from base months whose indices are not supplied"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the adjusted amounts of section 9(c2) need the index readings and they were not supplied` MEANS
    REFUSE "from 16 January 2028 section 9(c2) adjusts the amounts by the housing-services index, and the readings were not supplied"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 9(c1f) names a period whose end the sources give in two ways, and here it changes the answer` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 9(c1f) is printed as ending on 31 December 2024 and the consolidation's note says it was extended to 31 December 2026 by an order that is not deposited, and here the end of the period changes the answer"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 9(c2) does not say where a half of 5 shillings goes, and here it changes the answer` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 9(c2) rounds to the nearest multiple of 5 shillings and does not say where a half goes, and here it changes the answer"

-- The bands, from the lowest. A band is its top (NOTHING for the last) and its rate.
GIVEN u IS A NUMBER
      r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A band of a marginal scale`
`a purchase-tax band to` u `at` r MEANS
    `A band of a marginal scale` WITH
        `upper limit of the band` IS JUST u
        `rate of the band`        IS r

GIVEN r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A band of a marginal scale`
`the last purchase-tax band at` r MEANS
    `A band of a marginal scale` WITH
        `upper limit of the band` IS NOTHING
        `rate of the band`        IS r

-- (c1c)(1): the bands for an apartment bought by anyone, as printed for 2025.
@ref Real Estate Taxation Law s 9(c1c)(1) (source lines 193-198)
`retl 9(c1c)(1) — the bands printed for 2025` MEANS
    LIST `a purchase-tax band to` 1_465_800 `at` (5%),
         `a purchase-tax band to` 4_397_380 `at` (6%),
         `a purchase-tax band to` 6_055_070 `at` (7%),
         `a purchase-tax band to` 20_183_565 `at` (8%),
         `the last purchase-tax band at` (10%)

-- (c1c)(2)(3): the bands for an individual resident in Israel buying his only or a replacement apartment, as printed for 2025.
@ref Real Estate Taxation Law s 9(c1c)(2)(3) (source lines 213-218)
`retl 9(c1c)(3) — the bands printed for 2025` MEANS
    LIST `a purchase-tax band to` 1_978_745 `at` (0%),
         `a purchase-tax band to` 2_347_040 `at` (3.5%),
         `a purchase-tax band to` 6_055_070 `at` (5%),
         `a purchase-tax band to` 20_183_565 `at` (8%),
         `the last purchase-tax band at` (10%)

-- (c1f)(1): the bands for the investor, as printed for 2025.
@ref Real Estate Taxation Law s 9(c1f)(1) (source lines 234-237)
`retl 9(c1f) — the bands printed for 2025` MEANS
    LIST `a purchase-tax band to` 6_055_070 `at` (8%),
         `the last purchase-tax band at` (10%)

-- The tax by the bands on a value: each part of the value in a band at that band's rate.
@ref Real Estate Taxation Law s 9(c1c)-(c1f) (source lines 193-237)
GIVEN `the value` IS A NUMBER
      bands       IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`retl 9 — the purchase tax on a value of` `the value` `by the bands` bands MEANS
    `the tax of the layer through` bands `from the lower limit` 0 `for the layer from` 0 `to` `the value` `with each rate at most` `these rates are percentages, and nothing in the scale exceeds a hundred percent`

-- (c2): an amount adjusted by the rise of the index over the base index, rounded to the nearest multiple of 5 shillings.
@ref Real Estate Taxation Law s 9(c2) (source line 239); fork R2
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      ix     IS AN `Index readings for the amounts of section 9(c1c)`
      r      IS A `A reading of rounding to a multiple of 5 shillings`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`retl 9(c2) — the amount` amount `adjusted by` ix `and rounded to a multiple of 5, reading a half as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `a half goes up`    THEN `up`
    WHEN `a half goes down`  THEN `down`
    WHEN `declined where the rounding of a half changes the answer`
      THEN IF   `up` EQUALS `down`
           THEN `up`
           ELSE `section 9(c2) does not say where a half of 5 shillings goes, and here it changes the answer`
    WHERE
        `the adjusted amount` MEANS amount TIMES ix's `the new index, last published before the update day` DIVIDED BY ix's `the base index, published on 15 January 2027`
        `up`   MEANS 5 TIMES FLOOR (`the adjusted amount` DIVIDED BY 5 PLUS 0.5)
        `down` MEANS 5 TIMES CEILING (`the adjusted amount` DIVIDED BY 5 MINUS 0.5)

-- The bands with every upper limit adjusted.
GIVEN bands IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      ix    IS AN `Index readings for the amounts of section 9(c1c)`
      r     IS A `A reading of rounding to a multiple of 5 shillings`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
`retl 9(c2) — the bands` bands `adjusted by` ix `, reading a half as` r MEANS
    map (GIVEN b YIELD
            `A band of a marginal scale` WITH
                `upper limit of the band` IS (CONSIDER b's `upper limit of the band`
                                              WHEN JUST u  THEN JUST (`retl 9(c2) — the amount` u `adjusted by` ix `and rounded to a multiple of 5, reading a half as` r)
                                              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING)
                `rate of the band`        IS b's `rate of the band`)
        bands

-- (c1c)(2): the buyer pays by the bands of (3) if he is an individual resident in Israel and one of (a), (b), (b1), (c) holds.
@ref Real Estate Taxation Law s 9(c1c)(2) (source lines 199-213)
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A `A purchase of a right in a residential apartment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`retl 9(c1c)(2) — the buyer pays by the bands of paragraph (3) for` `the purchase` MEANS
        `the purchase`'s `the buyer is an individual resident in Israel`
    AND (   `the purchase`'s `the apartment is the buyer's only apartment`
         OR `the purchase`'s `the buyer sold the other apartment that was his only one within the period`
         OR `the purchase`'s `the buyer bought the apartment after a purchase-group apartment was delayed, as (c1c)(2)(b1) says`
         OR `the purchase`'s `the apartment is a replacement apartment as section 49E(a) means`)

-- The bands that apply on the day, for an end of the (c1f) period named: (2)'s bands, (c1f)'s while its period runs, else (c1c)(1)'s.
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A `A purchase of a right in a residential apartment`
      `the end of the (c1f) period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
`retl 9 — the printed bands for` `the purchase` `if the (c1f) period ends on` `the end of the (c1f) period` MEANS
    IF   `retl 9(c1c)(2) — the buyer pays by the bands of paragraph (3) for` `the purchase`
    THEN `retl 9(c1c)(3) — the bands printed for 2025`
    ELSE IF   `the purchase`'s `the day of the sale` AT LEAST YMD 2021 11 28 AND `the purchase`'s `the day of the sale` AT MOST `the end of the (c1f) period`
         THEN `retl 9(c1f) — the bands printed for 2025`
         ELSE `retl 9(c1c)(1) — the bands printed for 2025`

-- The tax on a purchase: the bands printed for the tax years 2025 to 2027 (16 January 2025 to 15 January 2028), adjusted by the index from 16 January 2028.
@ref Real Estate Taxation Law s 9(c1c), (c1f), (c2) (source lines 193-239); forks P1, R2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A `A purchase of a right in a residential apartment`
      ix             IS A MAYBE (`Index readings for the amounts of section 9(c1c)`)
      p1             IS A `A reading of the end of the period of section 9(c1f)`
      r2             IS A `A reading of rounding to a multiple of 5 shillings`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`retl 9 — the purchase tax on` `the purchase` `, the index readings being` ix `, reading the end of (c1f) as` p1 `and the rounding of a half as` r2 MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the purchase`'s `the day of the sale` LESS THAN YMD 2025 1 16
            THEN `section 9 as deposited states the bands for a sale from 16 January 2025 on`
        IF `the purchase`'s `the day of the sale` AT LEAST YMD 2028 1 16
            THEN CONSIDER ix
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN `the adjusted amounts of section 9(c2) need the index readings and they were not supplied`
                 WHEN JUST readings
                   THEN `retl 9 — the purchase tax on a value of` (`the purchase`'s `the value of the right sold`) `by the bands` (`retl 9(c2) — the bands` (`retl 9 — the printed bands for` `the purchase` `if the (c1f) period ends on` (YMD 2024 12 31)) `adjusted by` readings `, reading a half as` r2)
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER p1
            WHEN `the period ends on 31 December 2024, as the paragraph prints it`
              THEN `the tax if it ends in 2024`
            WHEN `the period ends on 31 December 2026, as the consolidation's note on the extension says`
              THEN `the tax if it ends in 2026`
            WHEN `declined where the end of the period changes the answer`
              THEN IF   `the tax if it ends in 2024` EQUALS `the tax if it ends in 2026`
                   THEN `the tax if it ends in 2024`
                   ELSE `section 9(c1f) names a period whose end the sources give in two ways, and here it changes the answer`
    WHERE
        `the tax if it ends in 2024` MEANS
            `retl 9 — the purchase tax on a value of` (`the purchase`'s `the value of the right sold`) `by the bands` (`retl 9 — the printed bands for` `the purchase` `if the (c1f) period ends on` (YMD 2024 12 31))
        `the tax if it ends in 2026` MEANS
            `retl 9 — the purchase tax on a value of` (`the purchase`'s `the value of the right sold`) `by the bands` (`retl 9 — the printed bands for` `the purchase` `if the (c1f) period ends on` (YMD 2026 12 31))
